1
00:00:05,020 --> 00:00:05,850
Aaaaaaah!

2
00:00:05,933 --> 00:00:06,763
It's Rob Luffy!

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:08,320
Then it's true.

4
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:11,977
They came here to kill Vegapunk
just as he feared that they would.

5
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:14,137
Who the hell invited you pigeon guy?

6
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:15,396
You get out of here!

7
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:20,640
This is a government island.

8
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:22,277
Oh, crap, you're right.

9
00:00:22,360 --> 00:00:24,377
We're the ones who aren't
supposed to be here.

10
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:25,580
Ah! Will you focus?

11
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:27,015
None of that matters!

12
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:28,500
Come on, Luffy.

13
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:30,557
We've got to get to the upper level now.

14
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:31,940
The Straw Hats, huh?

15
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,871
Didn't know this place had a pest problem.

16
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:36,360
Jewelry Bonnie, too.

17
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:39,340
But we can't do anything yet, Luchi.

18
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:42,577
Remember, Straw Hat is an
emperor of the sea now.

19
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:45,117
We can't fight him without
permission from the top.

20
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:46,030
He's right.

21
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:49,007
The four emperors often
have powerful allies.

22
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:51,774
One little scuffle could lead to a war.

23
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:54,200
Send a report to the Navy now. Roger!

24
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:57,620
I'm not sure we can
avoid a fight so easily.

25
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:04,100
Gotta go, Jinbei. Hold on to you.

26
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:14,131
Huffy, what's the matter?

27
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,060
What happened?

28
00:01:18,180 --> 00:01:19,440
Wait, I know her.

29
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:21,840
It's that girl from before.

30
00:01:22,380 --> 00:01:24,060
Chopper, help her, please.

31
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:29,260
I'm sorry, though.

32
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:32,540
I think this is more
Frankie's specialty than mine.

33
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:42,520
This is government business.

34
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:45,018
You would be wise to stay out of it.

35
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:48,420
She fed us!

36
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:52,501
She took care of us when we came
here, and that makes her a friend!

37
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:33,217
Actually,

38
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:34,617
don't

39
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:41,700
limit.

40
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:06,500
Thank you.

41
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:33,540
The Straw Hats are on Egghead!

42
00:03:33,740 --> 00:03:34,840
Why, damn it?

43
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:36,160
See this.

44
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:40,585
You give people an engine, they
give you nothing but a headache.

45
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:44,057
They must have figured out that
CP0 was there to kill them.

46
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:46,220
That's not a good sign. Yes, sir.

47
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:49,911
That's likely why they had to
use Esper to teleport inside.

48
00:03:50,900 --> 00:03:53,700
What they did is declare war!

49
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:57,698
Wish they'd had the common
sense to contact me first!

50
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:59,340
Those arrogant brats.

51
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:04,057
If Vegapunk has the Straw Hats on his
side, this could be a real disaster.

52
00:04:04,140 --> 00:04:06,846
Who knows how many good
marines we could lose.

53
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:09,500
Where's Kizaru?

54
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:12,337
He's on his way to Egghead right now!

55
00:04:12,420 --> 00:04:15,497
He was already en route, in
service of a different mission.

56
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:19,580
Tell Luchi to avoid any further
action until backup arrives.

57
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:25,300
No matter what happens, we
cannot let him fight Straw Hat!

58
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:30,700
Entruder alert!

59
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:32,315
Evacuate immediately!

60
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:34,500
I repeat, evacuate immediately!

61
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:43,857
Hey! Yoo-hoo! Pigeon guy!

62
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:45,500
Get over here!

63
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:47,000
Let's fight some more!

64
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:56,931
I'm still playing games even
when your life is on the line.

65
00:04:57,740 --> 00:04:59,840
I'm starting to get annoyed.

66
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,060
Don't get cocky, Straw Hat.

67
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:36,060
I've gotten stronger just like you have.

68
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:38,929
All the better to eat
prey like you, alive.

69
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:43,857
Wait, something's different.

70
00:05:43,940 --> 00:05:46,469
He definitely didn't
look like that before.

71
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:48,980
Stop, Blue Chief!

72
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:51,456
We don't have authorization for this!

73
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:58,960
His speed is incredible,
but so is his control.

74
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:03,558
It's rare that an Awakened Snow user
can maintain their state of mind.

75
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:22,430
It's mine!

76
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:35,510
Susie!

77
00:06:35,593 --> 00:06:36,837
Susie, you're out of control!

78
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:38,577
Please think of the position you're in!

79
00:06:38,660 --> 00:06:41,189
The government will
hunt you down for this!

80
00:06:49,660 --> 00:06:50,490
Shaka!

81
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:51,460
What happened?

82
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:53,597
Did the Whitehead Fight appear?

83
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:55,277
Oh my god, real Vegapunk!

84
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:57,713
How the hell did he get up here so fast?

85
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:00,730
Remarkable!

86
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:04,866
Tell me more, I must know everything
about this transformation.

87
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:06,440
What is that form?

88
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:09,037
Well, it's new, so we
don't know much either.

89
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:11,002
But it's a Gum-Gum thing, right?

90
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:19,980
In the Devil Fruit encyclopedia, there
is no mention of a Gum-Gum fruit.

91
00:07:20,220 --> 00:07:22,000
This must be something else.

92
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:23,390
Huh?

93
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:26,257
Wait, are you saying it's
a different Devil Fruit?

94
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:29,752
If that's true, then why does
he say Gum-Gum all the time?

95
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:34,820
He's so beautiful.

96
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:39,440
There is a figure from the ancient past.

97
00:07:39,840 --> 00:07:42,780
One with the same form
your captain has now.

98
00:07:43,940 --> 00:07:46,800
A god from the old texts?

99
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:48,420
A god?

100
00:07:48,620 --> 00:07:50,040
I'm sorry, Luffy?

101
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:51,693
Stupid incarnate Luffy?

102
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:54,710
Yes.

103
00:07:54,793 --> 00:07:56,620
The warrior of liberation.

104
00:07:57,100 --> 00:08:01,460
He who plays the fool
and brings smiles to all.

105
00:08:02,220 --> 00:08:04,600
There's no mistaking him.

106
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:07,680
He is the sun god, Nika!

107
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:11,820
Nika?

108
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:13,337
I've never heard of him.

109
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:17,557
That's no surprise, the world
government erased his name from history.

110
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:21,800
But as long as people yearn
for the warrior of liberation,

111
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,677
he will never truly disappear!

112
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:27,980
For it is desire that brings
forth everything in this world.

113
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:32,297
Take for example, the devil
fruits and all their power.

114
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:35,440
You can see it, can't you?

115
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:40,577
Each Devil Fruit is a
possibility for evolution

116
00:08:40,660 --> 00:08:43,820
that someone desires I
wish I could do this.

117
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:45,440
I wish I could do that.

118
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:49,232
All of the powers represent
potential futures of humanity.

119
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:54,180
But these fantastic possibilities
are not a natural part of this world.

120
00:08:54,460 --> 00:08:58,320
So the mother of nature,
the sea, rejects them.

121
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:02,340
Therefore, you might say...

122
00:09:05,340 --> 00:09:10,040
...soles who have powers
live in different realities.

123
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:13,900
Please, reality's someone dreamed of.

124
00:09:19,040 --> 00:09:20,960
That is my hypothesis.

125
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:25,960
Wonder God's existence is irrelevant.

126
00:09:27,660 --> 00:09:30,248
What an interesting
world, wouldn't you say?

127
00:09:36,140 --> 00:09:38,057
Do those idiots know
where they're fighting?

128
00:09:38,140 --> 00:09:40,100
This isn't a playground.

129
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:43,300
Not for pirates and not for CP0, either.

130
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:49,017
Why are you bothering me on my day off?

131
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:51,159
Why did you take so long to answer?

132
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:52,510
Whatever.

133
00:09:52,593 --> 00:09:53,518
I'm here, aren't I?

134
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:55,311
So what's the plan, punk?

135
00:09:55,780 --> 00:09:59,427
Cipher Pole is our ally, and the
pirates are the enemy, right?

136
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:02,760
Do you want me to just
back up CP0 or what?

137
00:10:03,420 --> 00:10:05,244
Quite the opposite, I'm afraid.

138
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:09,988
CP0 is here to assassinate me,
so I need your help to escape!

139
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:12,917
Don't get caught up in the details!

140
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,117
Just keep them away!

141
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:15,180
I can't do that!

142
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:17,616
Do you know what they do to traitors?

143
00:10:18,260 --> 00:10:19,120
You're right.

144
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:20,440
My apologies.

145
00:10:20,860 --> 00:10:22,272
But let me ask you this.

146
00:10:23,640 --> 00:10:24,470
Sentomaru?

147
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:27,420
Can't you do this one teensy favor for me?

148
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:29,360
The man who saved you?

149
00:10:29,620 --> 00:10:30,880
From poverty?

150
00:10:31,620 --> 00:10:33,340
All those years ago?

151
00:10:34,900 --> 00:10:36,720
Wow, no pressure, huh?

152
00:10:45,180 --> 00:10:46,880
Is he going to attack us?

153
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:49,740
Three Seraphim.

154
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:52,560
I'm not looking forward to this.

155
00:10:55,180 --> 00:10:56,886
Esper, pin out their numbers.

156
00:10:58,120 --> 00:10:59,840
Esper, don't move!

157
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:03,540
We can't beat them. Not like this.

158
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:05,160
Go, S-Bear!

159
00:11:05,380 --> 00:11:06,600
Take out CP-Zero!

160
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:07,799
They're the enemy!

161
00:11:13,220 --> 00:11:14,050
Retreat!

162
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:26,380
We need a new plan, and fast. No kidding.

163
00:11:27,140 --> 00:11:31,457
So the issue is that Saint Moria outranks
the authority chips we're carrying?

164
00:11:31,540 --> 00:11:32,370
That's right.

165
00:11:32,580 --> 00:11:34,756
The system of control is a hierarchy.

166
00:11:34,940 --> 00:11:36,917
If someone who's higher
ranked gives an order,

167
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,377
that's the order the Seraphim will follow.

168
00:11:39,460 --> 00:11:42,700
The highest on the authority
chain are the Five Elders.

169
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:47,960
The second highest is Dr. Vegapunk.

170
00:11:49,020 --> 00:11:51,120
The third is Saint Moria.

171
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,941
And authority chip holders
like us are the fourth.

172
00:11:56,960 --> 00:12:01,460
No matter what we do, Sintomaru's
commands will always be prioritized.

173
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:06,077
Then why don't we make a call to the
Five Elders and have them take control?

174
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:07,631
It doesn't work that way.

175
00:12:08,460 --> 00:12:11,017
Pacifistas have to receive
their commands directly.

176
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:15,840
They won't react to a transponder snail,
even if it is the Five Elders calling.

177
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:19,957
Then what are we supposed to do?

178
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:22,257
The Seraphim are valuable
government property.

179
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:23,557
We can't just destroy them.

180
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:24,820
Darn it, Luchy!

181
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:27,136
You really didn't think this through.

182
00:12:45,680 --> 00:12:46,960
You ready?

183
00:12:49,180 --> 00:12:50,220
Go, go!

184
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:52,470
Move!

185
00:12:58,880 --> 00:13:00,300
Time to do this.

186
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:04,617
First, S-Snake, guide Straw Hat and
his friends to the vacuum rocket.

187
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:07,171
They need to make it to the frontier dome.

188
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:11,300
S-Hawk, S-Shark, hold Cape back.

189
00:13:12,060 --> 00:13:14,884
Chopper, do those children
look familiar to you?

190
00:13:15,300 --> 00:13:17,477
Apart from the Black Wings and the Flames,

191
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:20,237
they all look like former
warlords of the sea.

192
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:21,150
You're right.

193
00:13:21,340 --> 00:13:23,458
There's no way that's a coincidence.

194
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:26,520
The government must have
made clones out of us.

195
00:13:28,220 --> 00:13:29,640
Hey, Axe Guy!

196
00:13:33,060 --> 00:13:35,000
It's been a while, old buddy.

197
00:13:36,140 --> 00:13:37,260
Straw Hat.

198
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:41,057
Current circumstances aside,
you and I are enemies.

199
00:13:41,140 --> 00:13:42,420
And I have a name.

200
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:45,440
So what, you're helping Punk escape?

201
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:46,915
Do I have that right?

202
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:50,140
Uh-huh, I like his apple
head, and he asked.

203
00:13:50,480 --> 00:13:53,480
Well, that doesn't exactly
fill me with confidence.

204
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:55,816
But I suppose you are an emperor now.

205
00:14:05,380 --> 00:14:06,660
Hand pistol.

206
00:14:12,460 --> 00:14:13,680
Black Sky!

207
00:14:14,940 --> 00:14:17,280
That takes care of their commander.

208
00:14:18,140 --> 00:14:21,080
Seraphim, you follow our orders now.

209
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:24,920
I'm sorry!

210
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:27,480
I just got to do it! Now you're dead!

211
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:29,790
Idiot.

212
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:32,400
You didn't distract me.

213
00:14:32,660 --> 00:14:34,440
I saw that hit coming.

214
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:43,000
Damn it!

215
00:14:43,540 --> 00:14:49,937
I was

216
00:14:50,020 --> 00:14:50,960
so sure.

217
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:53,020
I'm locked in time.

218
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:04,120
Hurry up and die?

219
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,840
I can't take control
until you're unconscious!

220
00:15:46,760 --> 00:15:49,357
I'm sure you thought
you had a fine strategy.

221
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:51,857
overriding our orders to the Seraphim.

222
00:15:51,940 --> 00:15:55,200
But all you did was put a
nail in your own coffin!

223
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:20,280
Gum-Gum!

224
00:16:24,280 --> 00:16:25,110
John!

225
00:16:26,340 --> 00:16:27,170
John!

226
00:16:40,340 --> 00:16:41,320
Lucci.

227
00:16:44,020 --> 00:16:45,420
Whoa!

228
00:16:48,180 --> 00:16:49,720
Now's our chance!

229
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:51,270
Hurry, Loopy!

230
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:53,117
If we want to save this girl's life,

231
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:56,057
then we have to get to
Vegapunk's lab immediately!

232
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:59,780
I mean, it's not like I
don't want to, but, uh...

233
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,960
I can't stop spinning!

234
00:17:17,060 --> 00:17:21,180
Whoa, you really can't stop spinning,
have it to go, Doctor, quick!

235
00:17:21,500 --> 00:17:23,794
Sorry, it gives up someone underground!

236
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:25,390
Oh, no!

237
00:17:25,820 --> 00:17:26,650
Oh, no!

238
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:31,280
To the factory! Hurry!

239
00:18:00,620 --> 00:18:03,337
Is there nothing we can
do to stop these things?

240
00:18:03,420 --> 00:18:05,538
We're losing men to our own weapons!

241
00:18:05,780 --> 00:18:09,368
I shudder to imagine how strong
they'll be once they grow up.

242
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:11,560
Hey, Vegapunk!

243
00:18:13,620 --> 00:18:14,450
What's wrong?

244
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:16,230
Tell me the truth.

245
00:18:16,313 --> 00:18:17,440
What is that power?

246
00:18:17,580 --> 00:18:20,597
And what the hell is that
Jinbei thing doing with it?

247
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:23,504
Guess that looks like the
Swim Swim fruit to me.

248
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:25,288
What's the Swim Swim fruit?

249
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:26,710
It's his.

250
00:18:26,793 --> 00:18:30,876
My hard-boiled brother from another
mother, Sonar Pink, has that power.

251
00:18:31,380 --> 00:18:33,020
I'd recognize it anywhere.

252
00:18:38,940 --> 00:18:41,897
But it's impossible for
there to be two of the same

253
00:18:41,980 --> 00:18:45,517
Devil Fruit so that means
my Bro must have died

254
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:50,717
but

255
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:52,957
he's

256
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:58,317
not dead he's just being
held in impel down hold up

257
00:18:58,400 --> 00:19:02,000
Does that mean you found a
way to duplicate devil fruits

258
00:19:03,620 --> 00:19:06,820
Well, some devil fruits can be copied

259
00:19:10,180 --> 00:19:13,200
But it only works with Snow types

260
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:21,565
Though the less said about caesar's
smile experiments the better

261
00:19:22,040 --> 00:19:23,922
Yeah, he can go straight to hell

262
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:29,637
The smiles offer a high
risk and low success

263
00:19:29,720 --> 00:19:32,580
rate They only work one time out of ten,

264
00:19:32,780 --> 00:19:36,537
and those who aren't granted power
never stop smiling or laughing.

265
00:19:36,620 --> 00:19:38,937
They can't even mourn for
their lost loved ones.

266
00:19:39,020 --> 00:19:39,900
It's sick.

267
00:19:41,140 --> 00:19:41,970
Caesar.

268
00:19:42,053 --> 00:19:45,093
Just hearing his name again
makes me want to blow chunks.

269
00:19:48,100 --> 00:19:50,571
Aberrations such as those notwithstanding.

270
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:52,980
I have not given up.

271
00:19:53,320 --> 00:19:55,760
If we had enough funding and enough time,

272
00:19:55,940 --> 00:19:59,100
we could replicate any
Devil Fruit in the world.

273
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:03,820
No, I'm not sure if the hell awaken.

274
00:20:11,340 --> 00:20:15,140
I've tried to recreate Logia
powers, but I've had no luck.

275
00:20:16,340 --> 00:20:19,740
And yet, for a Paramecia fruit,

276
00:20:19,980 --> 00:20:23,274
I need only acquire the
bloodline elements of its owner.

277
00:20:23,380 --> 00:20:27,440
Then I can synthesize a special
compound which, when administered,

278
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:30,742
confers the devil's root
power to another person.

279
00:20:35,260 --> 00:20:36,090
Observe.

280
00:20:36,560 --> 00:20:40,240
That's the fluid you see flowing
through the seraphim's arms.

281
00:20:41,180 --> 00:20:42,900
The green blood.

282
00:20:45,680 --> 00:20:46,660
Hold up!

283
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:48,626
You made a new kind of blood?

284
00:20:51,700 --> 00:20:53,000
Love, love?

285
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:10,660
I believe that Seraphim represents the
pinnacle of modern scientific possibilities.

286
00:21:13,800 --> 00:21:15,780
Where's the shock go?

287
00:21:22,900 --> 00:21:25,560
Do you know what that makes them?

288
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:29,700
It's the strongest form
of humanity in history.

289
00:21:30,560 --> 00:21:33,077
Is that why the government
got rid of them?

290
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:37,937
Why the hell would you even make something
stronger than a warlord, you psychopath?

291
00:21:38,020 --> 00:21:41,560
They're navy weapons
killing machines. Yes.

292
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:44,647
And sooner or later
they'll be aiming for us.

293
00:21:56,020 --> 00:21:57,220
Hold on, Sentomaru!

294
00:21:59,040 --> 00:22:00,000
Stay back!

295
00:22:01,720 --> 00:22:03,320
This isn't over yet.

296
00:22:16,560 --> 00:22:18,360
Sentomaru, please stay safe!

297
00:22:20,140 --> 00:22:23,300
Now where did that little
friend of yours run off to?

298
00:22:23,980 --> 00:22:25,140
I don't know.

299
00:22:26,020 --> 00:22:27,373
And he's not my friend!

300
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:29,040
What a shame.

301
00:22:29,340 --> 00:22:31,222
Guess you're all alone, traitor.

302
00:22:56,860 --> 00:22:59,880
Oh, my God.

303
00:23:29,380 --> 00:23:30,880
Oh, boy!

304
00:23:31,040 --> 00:23:31,880
Oh!

305
00:23:47,120 --> 00:23:47,950
Watch it!

306
00:24:01,700 --> 00:24:03,880
Ha ha ha ha!

307
00:24:09,040 --> 00:24:10,300
Hee hee!

308
00:24:16,940 --> 00:24:19,120
Go! Go!

309
00:24:21,640 --> 00:24:23,800
Go on!

310
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:32,320
Rick!

311
00:24:36,580 --> 00:24:39,380
When did he get so powerful?

312
00:24:41,720 --> 00:24:43,300
Damn it!

313
00:24:45,940 --> 00:24:48,380
I'm losing consciousness!

314
00:25:01,040 --> 00:25:02,320
Follow me, quickly!

315
00:25:12,920 --> 00:25:14,380
I said hurry!

316
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:19,979
This is no time to be
dragging your feet, you fools!

317
00:25:20,660 --> 00:25:22,601
The vacuum rocket is right there!

318
00:25:23,800 --> 00:25:25,180
Now get on!

319
00:25:26,260 --> 00:25:27,400
Why, thank you!

320
00:25:27,680 --> 00:25:30,621
You know you're much kinder
than the real Hancock.

321
00:25:31,040 --> 00:25:32,240
We owe you one!

322
00:25:32,540 --> 00:25:33,820
Much of lies! What?

323
00:25:34,100 --> 00:25:35,394
Dude, don't be absurd!

324
00:25:35,600 --> 00:25:37,980
I'm just following orders, all right?

325
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:45,900
Vacuum rocket departing in one minute.

326
00:25:46,500 --> 00:25:47,457
Oh, wait, come on!

327
00:25:47,540 --> 00:25:48,599
We're out of time!

328
00:25:48,920 --> 00:25:50,220
Hurry up!

329
00:25:54,260 --> 00:25:55,720
What do I do?

330
00:25:56,160 --> 00:25:59,660
Attention, please take caution
while boarding the rocket.

331
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:03,830
Go!

332
00:26:04,160 --> 00:26:05,820
Then take care of punk!

333
00:26:06,140 --> 00:26:06,980
You hear me?

334
00:26:09,700 --> 00:26:10,530
Okay!

335
00:26:10,780 --> 00:26:11,662
Leave it to me!

336
00:26:14,240 --> 00:26:15,070
No!

337
00:26:15,200 --> 00:26:16,788
You're going the wrong way!

338
00:26:19,260 --> 00:26:20,090
Caution.

339
00:26:20,173 --> 00:26:22,420
Doors closing in ten seconds.

340
00:26:33,440 --> 00:26:35,734
We're going to get him off this island.

341
00:26:37,520 --> 00:26:39,920
No matter what, I promise.

342
00:26:51,400 --> 00:26:52,680
Doors closing.

343
00:26:59,100 --> 00:27:00,660
Prepare to launch.

344
00:27:06,420 --> 00:27:07,820
Isn't so neat?

345
00:27:15,740 --> 00:27:18,080
It's certainly something, all right!

346
00:27:18,920 --> 00:27:20,080
Where am I?

347
00:27:20,280 --> 00:27:21,809
What happened to Vegapunk?

348
00:27:22,680 --> 00:27:23,510
Huh?

349
00:27:24,580 --> 00:27:25,940
Where's pigeon guy?

350
00:27:26,180 --> 00:27:27,900
Let me out of the room! Whoa!

351
00:27:28,080 --> 00:27:29,137
Who the hell is this?

352
00:27:29,220 --> 00:27:30,867
It's Loopy, he's just tired!

353
00:27:31,020 --> 00:27:32,517
I'll give you the details later!

354
00:27:32,600 --> 00:27:34,129
How long was I passed out?

355
00:27:35,480 --> 00:27:37,460
Okay, maybe I'll get used to it!

356
00:27:37,860 --> 00:27:38,860
Don't go to farm!

357
00:27:39,080 --> 00:27:39,910
Please shut up!

358
00:27:39,993 --> 00:27:41,097
Easy does it!

359
00:27:41,180 --> 00:27:42,827
You'll shut up too, Grandpa!

360
00:27:42,920 --> 00:27:44,449
Go back to normal already!

361
00:27:47,640 --> 00:27:49,020
Departing Fabrio Base.

362
00:27:50,220 --> 00:27:51,600
Entering Lobby Base.

363
00:27:55,680 --> 00:27:59,497
Transit duration 32 seconds.

364
00:27:59,580 --> 00:28:03,077
You have arrived already.

365
00:28:03,160 --> 00:28:06,277
All subsequent rockets are cancelled.

366
00:28:06,360 --> 00:28:08,277
Lobby phase under Loguetown.

367
00:28:08,360 --> 00:28:10,740
Frontier dome security system engaged.

368
00:28:11,800 --> 00:28:13,617
Hostile intruder alert.

369
00:28:13,700 --> 00:28:19,880
All researchers evacuate to the factory
immediately and seal all entry points.

370
00:28:26,760 --> 00:28:28,760
Well, I will say this for the man.

371
00:28:31,020 --> 00:28:33,640
He was a faithful bodyguard to Vegapunk.

372
00:28:34,720 --> 00:28:36,340
Until his dying breath.

373
00:28:37,020 --> 00:28:38,120
Such a waste.

374
00:28:38,880 --> 00:28:41,233
Didn't have to end like this, Sentomaru.

375
00:28:41,340 --> 00:28:45,357
Need I remind you, our orders are to
wait for the Navy before making a move.

376
00:28:45,440 --> 00:28:47,517
They can twiddle their
thumbs all they like,

377
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:49,953
but I won't wait for Vegapunk to escape.

378
00:28:50,880 --> 00:28:53,477
What do they even stand
to gain from killing you?

379
00:28:53,560 --> 00:28:56,197
You're the smartest man in the
world, and you're on their side.

380
00:28:56,280 --> 00:28:59,045
If they do this, it'll
be a huge loss for them.

381
00:28:59,620 --> 00:29:00,700
Well, I think so.

382
00:29:00,880 --> 00:29:04,645
But it appears that the higher-ups
have a different perspective.

383
00:29:05,960 --> 00:29:10,397
I certainly made inventions that have
been beneficial to the world government.

384
00:29:10,480 --> 00:29:14,020
Innovations in navigation
technology using sea brism stones.

385
00:29:14,480 --> 00:29:16,180
Cyborg animal modifications.

386
00:29:17,520 --> 00:29:21,696
Not to mention my research on devil
fruits that unlocked their secrets.

387
00:29:21,840 --> 00:29:24,899
Or my creation of human
weapons with the pacifistas.

388
00:29:25,800 --> 00:29:29,280
And now, I've completed
the Seraphim as well.

389
00:29:30,300 --> 00:29:34,957
Now imagine if you thought I might turn
that frightful intelligence against you.

390
00:29:35,040 --> 00:29:36,280
Thought what you do.

391
00:29:36,560 --> 00:29:39,960
In that case, there's no choice. Hmm?

392
00:29:41,220 --> 00:29:42,050
I said.

393
00:29:42,260 --> 00:29:43,400
I will not.

394
00:29:43,540 --> 00:29:45,537
For the record, I never planned to revolt.

395
00:29:45,620 --> 00:29:48,208
I still need my research
funding, after all.

396
00:29:48,540 --> 00:29:52,260
But the powers that be decided
I was troubling that was that.

397
00:29:53,020 --> 00:29:54,667
Alas, life gives you lemons.

398
00:29:54,760 --> 00:29:56,357
Government tries to kill you for them.

399
00:29:56,440 --> 00:29:59,097
That is not how the expression
goes, and you know it!

400
00:29:59,180 --> 00:30:03,651
Just when I faced this quandary, an
emperor and his crew appeared before me.

401
00:30:03,880 --> 00:30:06,351
Fate brought us together, don't you think?

402
00:30:07,360 --> 00:30:08,190
Hold it!

403
00:30:08,273 --> 00:30:09,717
You mean you want to join our crew?

404
00:30:09,800 --> 00:30:11,520
Welcome aboard, crewmates!

405
00:30:12,500 --> 00:30:13,330
STURESUPER!

406
00:30:14,360 --> 00:30:16,948
Which of my babies do
you want to see first?

407
00:30:17,080 --> 00:30:18,160
The Sonny?

408
00:30:18,560 --> 00:30:19,840
General Franky?

409
00:30:20,640 --> 00:30:21,470
What?

410
00:30:21,553 --> 00:30:22,873
So we have to take him?

411
00:30:23,080 --> 00:30:24,360
Well, this sucks.

412
00:30:25,100 --> 00:30:26,500
Don't you worry, Nami!

413
00:30:26,800 --> 00:30:28,380
I'm on bodyguard duty.

414
00:30:28,700 --> 00:30:30,171
Oh, my, what a gentleman.

415
00:30:30,400 --> 00:30:33,500
Thank you, I feel much safer now. What?

416
00:30:33,720 --> 00:30:36,117
Shut up and unlock these
shitty shoes already!

417
00:30:36,200 --> 00:30:37,612
I wasn't talking to you!

418
00:30:38,060 --> 00:30:39,840
Oh, no! Atlas!

419
00:30:40,060 --> 00:30:40,890
This is serious!

420
00:30:40,973 --> 00:30:42,411
She's not boobing at all.

421
00:30:42,820 --> 00:30:44,620
Don't worry, we'll save you.

422
00:30:45,180 --> 00:30:46,997
Ready a repair session immediately.

423
00:30:47,080 --> 00:30:48,080
Patient incoming.

424
00:30:48,460 --> 00:30:49,897
Thank you for bringing her in.

425
00:30:49,980 --> 00:30:51,740
You can leave the rest to us.

426
00:30:52,300 --> 00:30:53,720
Of course. Good luck.

427
00:30:53,980 --> 00:30:55,333
Hey, screws for brains!

428
00:30:55,420 --> 00:30:57,008
Where the hell is Vegapunk?

429
00:30:57,640 --> 00:30:59,540
I know he's in here somewhere.

430
00:30:59,960 --> 00:31:01,160
Tell me now!

431
00:31:01,700 --> 00:31:02,740
Barney, stop it!

432
00:31:03,140 --> 00:31:04,660
You need to calm down.

433
00:31:07,520 --> 00:31:08,457
Wait a sec.

434
00:31:08,540 --> 00:31:10,420
Is this his lab?

435
00:31:11,640 --> 00:31:12,470
Wow!

436
00:31:12,553 --> 00:31:13,460
So cool!

437
00:31:14,060 --> 00:31:15,707
Are you seeing this, Bonnie?

438
00:31:16,860 --> 00:31:18,700
That ancient bastard!

439
00:31:19,260 --> 00:31:20,840
I'm gonna make him pay!

440
00:31:25,180 --> 00:31:26,010
Bonnie!

441
00:31:26,500 --> 00:31:28,029
Wait, where are you going?

442
00:31:31,640 --> 00:31:35,740
I told Vegapunk to turn my father
back to normal, and what did he do?

443
00:31:36,820 --> 00:31:38,740
He sicked bugs on me!

444
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:44,940
I'm going to bury him for this.

445
00:31:45,320 --> 00:31:48,026
I don't think the bugs
were his fault, though.

446
00:31:49,300 --> 00:31:50,300
Sonic, wait!

447
00:31:50,560 --> 00:31:52,089
We need to stick together!

448
00:31:52,300 --> 00:31:53,600
Hey, come back!

449
00:32:07,800 --> 00:32:10,537
Our authority chips are
finally back in effect.

450
00:32:10,620 --> 00:32:12,880
The Seraphim follow our orders now.

451
00:32:13,560 --> 00:32:15,501
Who's ready for a little revenge?

452
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:18,120
I took down one of the satellites.

453
00:32:19,880 --> 00:32:22,557
Including Vegapunk himself,
there are six more.

454
00:32:22,640 --> 00:32:24,120
This might not be easy.

455
00:32:24,560 --> 00:32:26,913
That's assuming we can even get to them.

456
00:32:27,300 --> 00:32:31,120
Trust me, that defense system
is nothing to scoff at.

457
00:32:33,080 --> 00:32:35,917
We'll see how long it
lasts against our forces.

458
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:37,717
Lock down the island.

459
00:32:37,800 --> 00:32:39,477
Destroy every last ship.

460
00:32:39,560 --> 00:32:42,137
You can find no one escapes.

461
00:32:42,220 --> 00:32:43,520
Egghead on our watch.

462
00:32:55,100 --> 00:32:57,797
The Straw Hats are protecting vagabond.

463
00:32:57,880 --> 00:32:59,300
How nice of them.

464
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:03,000
Well, I'm sure they'll be a big help.

465
00:33:05,360 --> 00:33:08,200
Too bad they still won't escape.

466
00:33:11,720 --> 00:33:15,120
They're in for one hell
of a surprise, after all.

467
00:33:17,020 --> 00:33:20,240
All right, proceed
according to plan, boys.

468
00:33:20,920 --> 00:33:23,300
Send every last ship we have

469
00:33:25,100 --> 00:33:27,100
to Egghead Island.

470
00:34:00,800 --> 00:34:03,600
Thank you.

471
00:34:30,980 --> 00:34:37,717
I'm laughing at the same time.

472
00:34:37,800 --> 00:34:40,540
I'm singing the same song.

473
00:34:41,480 --> 00:34:45,917
Even if I'm a teenager,

474
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:48,500
I don't want to forget.
